{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/23", "id": 5108226382, "node_id": "PR_kwDOVESuUM8AAAABMHlZTg", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/23", "diff_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/23.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/23.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/23", "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/23/commits", "review_comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/23/comments", "review_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/comments{/number}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/23/comments", "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/statuses/180cc37fa1d166743ccedb662fc353c4cd4bbe18", "number": 23, "state": "closed", "locked": false, "title": "Test reserved volume header bytes with a valid digest", "user": {"login": "aien-spark", "id": 330927100, "node_id": "U_kgDOE7mL_A", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/330927100?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark", "html_url": "https://github.com/aien-spark", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "### Problem\n\n`ginux_volume_format::decode` rejects a sector whose reserved header bytes\n(`RESERVED_OFFSET..HEADER_SIZE`, bytes 64..72) are nonzero. No test covers that\nguard. The existing corruption test changes a byte without recomputing the\ndigest, so the SHA-256 check rejects the sector before the reserved bytes\nmatter. With the guard removed (and the then-unused `RESERVED_OFFSET` constant\nwith it), `cargo fmt --all -- --check`,\n`cargo clippy --package ginux-volume-format -- -D warnings` and\n`cargo test --package ginux-volume-format` all still pass.\n\n### Solution\n\nOne test in the existing `mod tests` of `crates/volume-format/src/lib.rs`.\nFor each reserved offset it sets the byte to 1, recomputes the digest with\n`digest_sector`, and asserts `decode` returns `None`. It first asserts the\nunmodified committed sector decodes. No production code changes.\n\nThe per-offset pattern is adapted from\n[aien-dev/aienux `store_v1_negative.rs` at edac0f1b](https://github.com/aien-dev/aienux/blob/edac0f1b14dcc469fceb18783aa92ff6d92645b2/crates/aienos-kernel/tests/store_v1_negative.rs#L315-L324)\n(Apache-2.0).\n\n### Testing\n\nRust 1.99.0 from `rust-toolchain.toml` (rustc b940084d7), aarch64 Linux host.\n\n| State | `cargo test --package ginux-volume-format` |\n|---|---|\n| `main` 759cf2e2 | ok, 4 passed |\n| with this test | ok, 5 passed |\n| guard removed, with this test | FAILED: new test, `offset 64`; the 4 existing tests pass |\n| guard removed, without this test | ok, 4 passed |\n| guard range ends at `HEADER_SIZE - 1` | FAILED: new test, `offset 71` |\n| guard range starts at `RESERVED_OFFSET + 1` | FAILED: new test, `offset 64` |\n| guard removed, test without the digest recompute | ok, 5 passed (the digest check alone rejects) |\n| restored | ok, 5 passed |\n\nAlso on the patched tree, all exit 0:\n\n```\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\ncargo clippy --package ginux-volume-format -- -D warnings\ncargo clippy --package ginux-volume-format --tests -- -D warnings\n```\n\nNot run: the full `make check` (x86_64 UEFI/none targets) and `make test` (QEMU).\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] Test-only change: one file, 13 added lines inside `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`\n- [x] No production code, dependency or `Cargo.lock` change\n- [x] `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `cargo clippy --package ginux-volume-format -- -D warnings` clean\n- [x] New test fails when the reserved-byte guard is removed or narrowed at either end\n- [ ] Full `make check` / `make test`: not run\n", "labels": [], "milestone": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "created_at": "2026-11-01T14:20:14Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-01T23:32:45Z", "closed_at": "2026-11-01T23:32:45Z", "merged_at": "2026-11-01T23:32:45Z", "merge_commit_sha": "1c626c2da2009eb42e6d3070bd6a468345c1411a", "assignee": null, "assignees": [], "requested_reviewers": [], "requested_teams": [], "head": {"label": "aien-spark:test/volume-format-reserved-bytes", "ref": "test/volume-format-reserved-bytes", "repo": {"id": 1441894417, "node_id": "R_kgDOVfGQEQ", "name": "ginux", "full_name": "aien-spark/ginux", "owner": {"login": "aien-spark", "id": 330927100, "node_id": "U_kgDOE7mL_A", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/330927100?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark", "html_url": "https://github.com/aien-spark", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aien-spark/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_ty